    "behavior": "A diurnal skink with smooth, shiny scales. Do not confuse it with the tiny snake-eyed skink (Ablepharus).",
    "conservation": "Biologically confirmed in the checklist. The discussion notes that the E. s. princeps sequence differs from E. s. pavimentatus — a revision may follow, but this page does not split the species. No global IUCN category is given here.",
