    "overview": "The Caucasian green lizard (Lacerta media) is a lacertid. Tarkhnishvili et al. 2026 treat it as a candidate species: it belongs to the monophyletic L. trilineata complex; separate status is indirectly supported by phylogeny and parapatry in western Anatolia, but the contact zone with the L. trilineata group remains unexplored (Ahmadzadeh et al. 2013). Cytochrome b difference from L. trilineata reaches 6.5%. That does not confirm species rank in this atlas. It occurs in central and eastern Anatolia, Iran, and the Caucasus; in Georgia it is widespread in semiarid habitats of the east and sporadic in the northwest. The figure is from Tmogvi village; barcodes are from Pantishara Gorge and Tmogvi. It is harmless to people.",
