    "overview": "The Caucasian brown frog (Rana macrocnemis) is biologically confirmed. Ishchenko (1978) and Tarkhnishvili et al. (1999, 2001) accept two parapatric subspecies in Georgia: R. m. macrocnemis and R. m. camerani; their ranges do not match Veith et al. (2003). The taxonomic status of R. m. camerani needs population-genomic work and formal rank may be revised — it remains a listed species here, with subspecies mentioned only as the paper does. Barcodes: Tabatskuri (camerani) and Bjolieti, Guria (macrocnemis). The checklist figure is Guria, Bjolieti.",
